geeklist.comment:
[q="JeffyJeff"][q="StormbringerGrey"]Strictly speaking we don't require that sellers tag their buyers, not everyone is comfortable with BGG formatting codes but it really is as simple as copy/pasting the code above and it is very, very helpful for both buyers and sellers when trying to review their transactions.[/q] fwiw it's not standard afaik but my vfm tool uses some heuristics to try to determine the buyer if not explicitly tagged as Bob said and mentioned in the [[VFM]] wiki.
See bullet 3 in the thread [thread=2715629][/thread] for a break down of those.[/q] Thanks Jeff. Next weekend I am going to update the header to include useful information in winding down the VFM, it will include a plea to sellers to tag their buyers and instructions for how to do that.
@Adolph, I just checked and Bonnie's purchased items are still listed and in the locations sited. That said, tracking by item number is unreliable, a good reason why sellers should tag their buyers.

